-- M3 fixes round 2, R2: dead code must not abort a guard.  `deadcode`
-- is never referenced by `main`; its stamped type head is `Option`
-- (pure), so the round-1 rule executed its body at definition time in
-- run mode and the malformed regex pattern aborted the whole script:
-- pre-fix, `tot run` on this file exits 1 (= ask; recorded in
-- dev/M3-FIXES-LOG.md as the mutation confirmation) while `tot check`
-- reports it clean.  Post-fix every user def is a lazy memoized thunk
-- in run mode, `deadcode` is never forced, and `tot run` exits 0 with
-- an empty stdout envelope (allow prints nothing): dev/gates.sh's
-- PASS-RUN-DEADCODE-ABORT.
def deadcode : Option (Div Bool) := some (Div Bool) (regexTest "a\\(" "aaa")
def main : IO Verdict := pureIO Verdict allow
